Task 4.2: End-to-end verification script. Discovered during manual exploration that the structured log ctx (order_id/status/to/subject) never renders in text output - no logback.xml in this repo, so log4cats' MDC-based context is dropped by the default pattern. Fixed by interpolating the distinguishing fields directly into the two log message strings (EmailClient.send, OrderStatusChangedConsumer.handleEvent) rather than working around it in the script; existing unit tests check the ctx map, not the message text, so unaffected. Added scripts/verify-order-status-changed.sh mirroring payment-service's verify-order-reserved-consumer.sh shape: docker compose up -d, pre-create topic, sbt run, publish one synthetic event per of the 3 statuses, grep the log for the matching send, confirm /health/ready stays 200 throughout. Ran it for real against local Kafka - all checks passed. Files: EmailClient.scala, OrderStatusChangedConsumer.scala, scripts/verify-order-status-changed.sh.
